          "id": "XPhQD",
          "name": "Description",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A harness is a specialised module: a physical carrier of interface links between two or more modules. It is drawn as the carrier line itself, marked by a harness node that opens it like any other module (connectors, wires, length, artifacts). Every harness should stand for something physical: a cable, a bus backbone, a splice, a switch. Small squares mark the harness's own ports (its connector ends).",
