          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Modules with few interfaces show every port. Modules with many interfaces show one grouped port per interface type ('UART ×6') instead of cluttering the border; connecting one pops a concrete port out of the group. The visible set, grouping, and default side/position are configurable per module, and cards grow to fit their ports unless a geometry override sets size and shape. Proposal: port glyph shape encodes domain (circle electrical, square mechanical) so domain survives any colour classification.",
