                "YgzRP": {
                  "content": "Children exist (ModuleDef.children) and a harness endpoint that omits childModuleId implicitly means the parent's own interface (robot-car main_power), so boundary↔child links can be written. But the rule is implicit, instance-level endpoint bindings require a childModuleId, no engine code evaluates module-internal harnesses, and instantiateModule never builds childInstances. Needed: explicit endpoint target (self | child), recursion in instantiation, a module-scope evaluator."
                }
              }
